00:24:03.900 --> 00:24:07.660
- Washington Roebling was not seen on the bridge site again.

00:24:07.660 --> 00:24:09.330
He survived the caisson disease,

00:24:09.330 --> 00:24:11.750
but he never really recovered.

00:24:11.750 --> 00:24:14.710
He remained a recluse, suffering from pain,

00:24:14.710 --> 00:24:16.840
nervousness, failing eyesight,

00:24:16.840 --> 00:24:19.280
and terrible physical weakness.

00:24:19.280 --> 00:24:23.040
- I'm an invalid, confined to the house,

00:24:23.040 --> 00:24:24.500
and minerals are the only things

00:24:24.500 --> 00:24:28.190
which do not tire or excite me.

00:24:28.190 --> 00:24:30.000
- For the duration of the construction,

00:24:30.000 --> 00:24:34.020
Roebling lived on Brooklyn Heights, where he could supervise the work from his bedroom

00:24:34.020 --> 00:24:40.120
window, and it was from there that he transmitted his detailed instructions through Emily.

00:24:40.120 --> 00:24:45.100
It could not have been accomplished but for the unselfish devotion of his assistant engineers.

00:24:45.100 --> 00:24:49.420
Each man had a certain department in charge, and they worked with all their energies to

00:24:49.420 --> 00:24:54.540
have the job done properly, according to Colonel Roebling's plans and wishes.

00:24:54.540 --> 00:24:59.600
The average age of the engineering staff, Roebling included, was all of 31 years.

00:25:00.380 --> 00:25:06.030
Colonel William Payne at 41 was the old man of the staff, while George McNulty was barely

00:25:06.030 --> 00:25:11.080
20.

00:25:11.080 --> 00:25:16.960
February 1875, the work that should be pressed forward with all dispatch is the New York

00:25:16.960 --> 00:25:21.860
Anchorage, in order that it be completed by the time the masonry of the towers is ready

00:25:21.860 --> 00:25:30.000
for cable making.

00:25:30.030 --> 00:25:36.030
900 feet inland on both shores, two massive stone anchorages would be constructed to secure

00:25:36.030 --> 00:25:42.690
the ends of the four great suspension cables. The cables would be fixed to chains of long

00:25:42.690 --> 00:25:48.850
iron eye bars that disappeared into the anchorage and were in turn tied to four cast iron anchor

00:25:48.850 --> 00:25:55.740
plates embedded deep within the granite. When I place a certain amount of dead weight

00:25:55.740 --> 00:26:00.000
in the shape of granite on the anchor plates, I know it will remain

00:26:00.000 --> 00:26:12.850
there beyond all contingency. In 1871, the notorious William Marcy Tweed was New York's

00:26:12.850 --> 00:26:17.090
