00:28:30.890 --> 00:28:36.700
Cables, 1876 to 1878.

00:28:36.700 --> 00:28:39.720
As John Roebling had intended, the four main suspension

00:28:39.720 --> 00:28:43.870
cables would be constructed in place high above the river.

00:28:43.870 --> 00:28:46.650
Number eight gauge wires, less than a quarter of an inch

00:28:46.650 --> 00:28:48.890
in diameter, would be pulled strand by strand

00:28:48.890 --> 00:28:52.090
from great spools fixed on the Brooklyn anchorage.

00:28:52.090 --> 00:28:54.750
Traveler rope would take the wire up and over the Brooklyn

00:28:54.750 --> 00:28:58.230
tower, out over the river, up and over the other tower,

00:28:58.230 --> 00:28:59.860
and down to the far anchorage.

00:29:00.120 --> 00:29:02.480
where it would be looped around the anchor chain

00:29:02.480 --> 00:29:05.080
and then return to the Brooklyn side.

00:29:05.080 --> 00:29:07.010
The wires were laid up parallel,

00:29:07.010 --> 00:29:09.860
like pencils bound by rubber bands.

00:29:09.860 --> 00:29:15.470
Each finished cable would contain 6,289 such wires,

00:29:15.470 --> 00:29:19.500
over 3,500 miles, bundled tightly together.

00:29:19.500 --> 00:29:24.000
331 wires to a strand, 19 strands to a cable.

00:29:44.430 --> 00:29:48.990
John Roebling Sons, Inc. had pioneered cable manufacture in America

00:29:48.990 --> 00:29:52.420
and was unquestionably the best in the business.

00:29:52.420 --> 00:29:57.070
But John Roebling Sons did not make the cables for the Brooklyn Bridge.

00:29:57.070 --> 00:29:59.920
Seizing an opportunity to display his integrity,

00:30:00.060 --> 00:30:03.560
Abram S. Hewitt, a trustee who also manufactured wire,

00:30:03.560 --> 00:30:08.610
stated that he would not bid on the cables and further would resign if Roebling's sons did.

00:30:08.610 --> 00:30:12.670
As you seem to be deeply impressed with Mr. Hewitt's action,

00:30:12.670 --> 00:30:15.890
I desire to say that his magnanimity is all a show,

00:30:15.890 --> 00:30:20.390
as the firm of Cooper and Hewitt have no facilities whatever for making steel wire.

00:30:20.390 --> 00:30:24.730
And if you receive a bid from a Mr. Haig of South Brooklyn,

00:30:24.730 --> 00:30:27.250
it will be well for you to investigate a little.

00:30:30.410 --> 00:30:39.110
The work of manufacturing the crucible steel wire is now in active progress at the factory of Mr. J. Lloyd Haig in South Brooklyn.

00:30:39.110 --> 00:30:45.970
It is a matter of great satisfaction that such a superior quality of wire is being furnished.

00:30:45.970 --> 00:30:54.230
On Thanksgiving of 1877, a small wire snapped.

00:30:54.230 --> 00:30:59.730
The incident seemed of little consequence, but Colonel Payne sent a section of the wire to Roebling.

00:31:00.380 --> 00:31:04.560
It is as brittle as glass. It is worthless and the most dangerous material that could

00:31:04.560 --> 00:31:09.100
be employed. Is this due to a wrong system of inspection or what is the reason in your

00:31:09.100 --> 00:31:15.570
opinion? Washington Roebling. As Roebling had forewarned, Haig had been submitting and

00:31:15.570 --> 00:31:20.230
resubmitting the same good wire for inspection while sending hundreds of rejected spools

00:31:20.230 --> 00:31:24.410
down to the bridge site. The distressing point in this affair is that

00:31:24.410 --> 00:31:30.000
all the rejected wire has been worked into the cables and cannot be removed. We know that

00:31:30.000 --> 00:31:35.300
This has been going on for two months, and the probability is that it extends as far back as last January.

00:31:37.360 --> 00:31:40.900
At Haig's expense, 150 wires were added to each cable.

00:31:41.900 --> 00:31:48.330
The trustees tried to keep the incident quiet and awarded the next contract for suspenders to John Roebling's sons.

00:31:50.450 --> 00:31:52.840
September 1880, Brooklyn Eagle.

00:31:53.110 --> 00:31:59.670
Mr. J. Lloyd Haig, who figured more or less in connection with the big bridge, is breaking boulders in Sing Sing.

00:32:02.560 --> 00:32:05.790
The health of Colonel Roebling is considerably improved,

00:32:05.790 --> 00:32:08.600
but he is still unable to leave his home.

00:32:08.600 --> 00:32:14.610
Although an invalid, his attention to the details of the bridge is as keen as ever,

00:32:14.610 --> 00:32:18.780
and all matters of importance pass under his revision.

00:32:18.780 --> 00:32:25.070
Man is, after all, a very finite being in capacities and powers of doing actual work.

00:32:25.070 --> 00:32:29.640
But when it comes to planning, one mind can, in a few hours,

00:32:30.000 --> 00:32:34.160
think out enough work to keep a thousand men employed for years.

00:32:34.160 --> 00:32:45.740
Roadway, 1878 to 1883.

00:32:45.740 --> 00:32:53.300
In 1879, at the 10-year mark, all that remained to be constructed was the superstructure,

00:32:53.300 --> 00:32:56.070
the roadway between the two cities.

00:32:56.070 --> 00:33:00.000
Everything that had gone before it, the caissons, the towers, the cables, and the anchorages

00:33:00.000 --> 00:33:03.050
all these were built to support and suspend the roadway.

00:33:03.050 --> 00:33:05.830
August 10th, 1881.

00:33:05.830 --> 00:33:08.880
A lighter load of steel arrived at the bridge dock yesterday,

00:33:08.880 --> 00:33:11.880
