00:33:39.660 --> 00:33:43.310
down also.

00:33:43.310 --> 00:33:46.830
The delays were incredible and embarrassing.

00:33:46.830 --> 00:33:52.530
The Board of Trustees, now run by several newly elected reformed politicians, was worried

00:33:52.530 --> 00:33:57.600
about bad press and eager to please the public with positive actions.

00:33:57.600 --> 00:34:00.000
But their urgency to complete the bridge was without any

00:34:00.000 --> 00:34:05.240
real interest for the bridge itself, and with little or no comprehension of the human effort

00:34:05.240 --> 00:34:12.650
that had brought the project this far. Many of them had never even met the chief engineer.

00:34:12.650 --> 00:34:17.770
I am convinced that at every possible point there is a weakness in the management of the

00:34:17.770 --> 00:34:23.630
Brooklyn Bridge. The engineering part of the structure, the most important, is in the hands

00:34:23.630 --> 00:34:30.000
of a sick man. He was the perfect scapegoat. He hadn't been seen at the bridge site

00:34:30.000 --> 00:34:36.140
for 11 years. Only the assistant engineers knew how crucial he was to the success of the bridge,

00:34:36.140 --> 00:34:44.600
that he still carried the entire responsibility. You must trust me insofar that the moment I am

00:34:44.600 --> 00:34:52.650
unable to do full justice to my duties as chief engineer, I shall give you ample warning. Finding

00:34:52.650 --> 00:35:00.000
no better excuse for the delays, several trustees attempted to remove Washington Roebling. They were, by the narrow

00:35:00.000 --> 00:35:06.600
of margins defeated. Probably one reason why perfect harmony did not exist in the

00:35:06.600 --> 00:35:13.560
board was that there were four candidates for governor on it. If the board of

00:35:13.560 --> 00:35:17.340
trustees had failed to remember that it was the bridge that mattered, Washington

00:35:17.340 --> 00:35:22.420
Roebling had not. He got his floor beams and for seven more months he quietly and

00:35:22.420 --> 00:35:30.000
carefully supervised the finishing work. Then in early May of 1883 the bridge was ready to carry

00:35:30.000 --> 00:35:35.530
its first passenger it was Emily Roebling she rode across in an open

00:35:35.530 --> 00:35:42.160
carriage carrying a rooster a symbol of victory the East River Bridge will be

00:35:42.160 --> 00:35:47.820
open to the public Thursday May 24th at 2 o'clock Colonel and Mrs. Washington A

00:35:47.820 --> 00:35:52.260
Roebling request the honor of your company after the opening ceremonies

00:35:52.260 --> 00:36:00.000
until 7 o'clock the completed bridge was so grand so stately

00:36:00.000 --> 00:36:06.280
and magnificent, such a source of pride that all was forgiven. The wire fraud, boss tweed,

00:36:06.280 --> 00:36:11.560
the delays and doubts, all the criticism of the chief engineer, all were swept away by

00:36:11.560 --> 00:36:18.060
the irrefutable fact of the bridge itself. The United City staged the greatest celebration

00:36:18.060 --> 00:36:23.890
ever seen in New York. Everybody had the day off. Every business closed. President Chester

00:36:23.890 --> 00:36:30.000
A. Arthur presided with some 50,000 others from out of town. Hundreds of thousands of

00:36:30.000 --> 00:36:36.340
New Yorkers and Brooklynites. After dark, 14 tons of fireworks exploded for more than an hour.

00:36:37.850 --> 00:36:40.850
And the chief engineer was at last the unchallenged hero.

00:36:45.040 --> 00:36:52.320
Low soul, seest thou not God's purpose from the first? The earth be spanned,

